35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems general-use spaces are far more successful, though older blocks often hide hazardous materials that cause delays.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My data confirms this; general rooms are overbooked while specialist ones sit idle, and outages cost us heavily in off-site hire.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"We have a staffing crisis in grounds and front-of-house, yet technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks the equipment should handle.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Weather and ""comfort-based"" rationales are killing our schedules. We are losing weeks to rain and months to poor planning.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Mechanical costs are rising sharply, and we have a worrying lack of reserves for replacing aging audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"If we want a project that actually lands well, we should avoid narrow, single-wing benefits.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,And we must avoid any plan that removes critical room capacity without a viable internal alternative.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,A project that automates manual routines for our technicians would be a significant relief to the staff.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"We should avoid outdoor work or projects based on ""appeal,"" as they are the most likely to slip.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,I suggest we steer clear of expensive mechanical plant upgrades unless the budget is exceptionally robust.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
